Subject: [PATCH 3/5] launcher: the binary-override GGML strip keeps the role's
 own declared knobs (DAR-LAT-3h, PROPOSED)

Bug, found preparing DAR-LAT-3h. _apply_runtime_requirements_env strips every
GGML_* key except GGML_IQK whenever a binary override is set, to keep AMBIENT
knobs out of a binary that may not honour them. Since v10 every role has a
binary_dir (the kernel store), so _stack_prior_runtime_overrides always
returns an override and the strip always fires, including on the role's own
stack_env block. Evidence: the live :8074 (launched 2026-09-24, when
architect_critic still declared GGML_NUMA_REPACK_INTERLEAVE=0) carries no such
key in /proc/2030855/environ. Without this fix the recipe env in the next
lane commit would never reach the process either (demonstrated: the strip
prints ['GGML_NOHUGEPAGE_PROCESS', 'GGML_FA_SPLIT_KV', 'GGML_FUSED_DECODE_OFF']).
Lands in EVERY outcome of the DAR-LAT-3h gate: today no role declares a GGML
knob beyond GGML_IQK, so it changes no live env on its own.

- New `preserve` parameter: keys the role declares survive the strip; ambient
  GGML_* is still removed (build_launch_env already overwrote any ambient
  value of a declared key).
- start_server's registry-backed path passes the role's block. No role
  declares a GGML knob beyond GGML_IQK at this commit, so no role's env
  changes (test).
- New test_launch_env_strip_preserve.py: ambient stripped, declared kept,
  no-preserve behaviour unchanged, block-less roles unchanged.

Unsigned. Part of the DAR-LAT-3h stack-change package
(epyc-root artifacts/operator/stack-change-dar-lat-3h-20260926/).

